    "Opened on 12 September 2003, the Warnow Tunnel became Germany's first modern toll road, inaugurated by Transport Minister Dr. Manfred Stolpe amid a historic private financing deal in.",
    "Built using immersed‑tube construction, the tunnel features six prefabricated concrete conduits that were floated from a drydock, then lowered into a dredged channel beneath the Warnow River.",
    "By 2006, the Warnow Tunnel faced near bankruptcy after only 10,500 vehicles crossed daily—half the projected 20,000—prompting a concession extension from 30 to 50 years to boost profitability."
